.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-auth-login - Sign in to Microsoft Teams with a browser or a device code


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams auth login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in with the authorization code + PKCE flow in your browser, or with a
device code (\fB--device\fR) on a headless machine. When no terminal is available
the device-code flow is chosen automatically.

.PP
The MSAL token cache is written to the profile's token store: encrypted with a
key from your OS keychain by default, or a 0600 plaintext file where no
keychain is reachable.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--device\fP[=false]
	use the device-code flow instead of the browser

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--scopes\fP=""
	override the profile's scopes (a preset name or a space separated list)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-auth(1)\fP
